// The universal demo's layout kit.
//
// The components are NOT privileged. This is an ordinary tutucard — the same
// file shape a person or a model writes, compiled by the same `tgc/emit` and
// registered by the same `register_module` under the same policy — and the one
// place it differs is CONSTRUCTION: it is embedded rather than fetched, so the
// page has a palette before it has drawn anything.
//
// That is the whole demonstration. A host-provided component and a loaded
// guest have to be indistinguishable to the person and to every other guest,
// and the honest way to show it is to have no host-provided components at all.
//
// What lives here beside the card is the half a card manifest cannot carry:
// keywords, a category and presets. `tgc/emit` writes both fields empty and
// the card spec block has no syntax for either, so the SHIPPER supplies them —
// which is also how a card somebody pastes in gets found by name and doc alone.
import {
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/tgc/emit",
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/compose/catalog",
  "moonbitlang/core/json",
}
